#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
High-performance image selector with async loading, thumbnail caching,
lazy directory scanning, and multi-select support. (Qt port)

Usage:
    sel_img.py [directory...] [-r] [-t]
    -r  : recursively search subdirectories
    -t  : sort by modification time (newest first)

Dmenu mode:
    sel_img.py --dmenu-mode --list-file FILE --image-file FILE
    sel_img.py --dmenu-mode --list-entries "a\nb" --image-entries "1.png\n2.png"
    --return-label  : output the label instead of the image path (dmenu only)

Multi-select:
    <Control-Return>  : select / deselect current item
    <Return>          : confirm — prints all selected items + current item

Views:
    <Control-g>       : toggle between list view and gallery view
    <Tab>             : toggle between list view and gallery view
    --gallery-rows N  : target number of gallery rows visible (default 3.5)
    --gallery-cols N  : target number of gallery columns visible
    --gallery-tile-size N : explicit gallery tile size in pixels (overrides rows/cols)
    --gallery-aspect N    : tile width/height ratio (default: auto-detected)

Pre-select:
    --pre-select "entry1\nentry2"      : pre-select labels at launch
    --pre-select-file FILE             : read pre-select labels from file

Performance design (see comments in the module):
  * Decode target sizes are quantised to SIZE_BUCKETS so that the list view,
    the gallery view, and small window resizes all reuse the same decode.
  * The on-disk WebP cache is OFF by default (opt in with SEL_IMG_DISK_CACHE=1);
    the analysis showed its synchronous writes dominated the worker threads.
  * One in-memory LRU of ready QPixmaps, keyed by (path, bucket).
  * A priority decode pool dedups by (path, bucket): a prefetch and a later
    real request for the same file share a single decode.
  * Worker threads never touch QPixmap/QImage; conversion happens on the GUI
    thread via a Qt queued signal.
"""

